# What stays out of the npm tarball — the CLI, the skills and the plugin files.
#
# A `files` allowlist in package.json would be one list instead of two, and vsce
# refuses to run at all when both it and .vscodeignore exist. So each artifact keeps
# its own ignore file, and this one exists rather than that.
#
# npm reads .gitignore only when this file is absent. Its presence is what lets
# out/ — gitignored, and the only thing anyone installs this for — into the tarball.

# Sources. out/ is what runs, and the maps point at .ts files that do not ship.
src/
test/
*.map
tsconfig.json
eslint.config.mjs

# For people reading the repository, not for anyone installing it. README.md is
# always included by npm and is the page this package shows.
docs/

# Live credentials. npm has no default opinion about .env, and a tarball is
# public and permanent.
.env
.env.*

# Tooling and editor state.
.github/
.vscode/
.claude/
.vscodeignore
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
*.vsix

# The activity-bar icon and the agent marks are used at runtime by the extension
# half of out/. The readme's screenshot is served from GitHub, not from here.
media/screenshot-review.png
